WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.413
The national security state.

00:00:02.363 --> 00:00:04.840
Surveillance without accountability.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:18.102
Canada's national security apparatus includes CSIS for domestic intelligence, the Communications Security Establishment for signals intelligence, the RCMP for law enforcement intelligence, and the Department of National Defence for military intelligence.

00:00:18.102 --> 00:00:25.772
Five oversight bodies monitor these agencies — NSICOP, NSIRA, the Federal Court, the Privacy Commissioner, and the Inspector General.

00:00:25.772 --> 00:00:27.727
None can enforce.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:35.090
As documented in the CSIS oversight analysis, all five can investigate, none can compel corrective action with binding authority.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:47.727
Meanwhile, surveillance powers have expanded through Bill C-59, the Emergencies Act powers demonstrated in 2022, and the three-bill surveillance architecture of C-63, C-8, and C-22.

00:00:47.727 --> 00:00:57.022
The pattern is consistent with every other layer of institutional capture: expand the power, maintain the appearance of oversight, ensure the oversight cannot enforce.

00:00:57.022 --> 00:01:00.806
The four pillars of Canada's national security apparatus.

00:01:00.806 --> 00:01:02.772
The oversight gap.

00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:05.829
Five bodies oversee national security.

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:07.784
None can enforce.

00:01:07.784 --> 00:01:10.863
The security layer of institutional capture.

00:01:10.863 --> 00:01:16.170
The national security state is the enforcement layer that ensures the captured system persists.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:20.420
When citizens protest, the Emergencies Act freezes their accounts.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.704
When journalists investigate, CSIS can monitor them without their knowledge.

00:01:24.704 --> 00:01:31.102
When whistleblowers speak, the PSDPA fails to protect them as documented in the whistleblower analysis.

00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:35.147
When Parliament demands documents, cabinet confidence blocks them.

00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:39.306
The security apparatus exists to protect the state from threats.

00:01:39.306 --> 00:01:45.647
When the state itself is the threat to democratic accountability, the security apparatus protects the threat from the people.

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:48.886
This is the final layer of the system architecture.

00:01:48.886 --> 00:01:52.409
It is the layer that ensures all other layers persist.
